/-!
# One family of component ideals: reduced, one-dimensional, and cut out by incidence

Let `X` be a decent algebraic space over `S`, let `x` be a point of it and write
`A = 𝒪^h_{X, x}` for the henselian local ring of Stacks 0ENK there. The additivity of the order
of vanishing over the irreducible components of `X` through `x`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.natCast_ord_sub_eq_finsum_components_mul_of_le_iff`, asks for a family of
ideals `I i ⊆ A` with three properties at once:

* `A ⧸ I i` is reduced,
* `ringKrullDim (A ⧸ I i) = 1`, and
* a branch `𝔮` of `A` contains `I i` exactly when the component it lies on is the `i`-th one.

The family `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_componentIdealFamily_isReduced_ringKrullDim_eq_one`
has the two ring-theoretic properties, because its ideals come with isomorphisms
`A ⧸ I i ≅ 𝒪^h_{X_i, ξ_i}`; the family
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_componentIdealFamily_le_iff_eq` has the incidence, because its
ideals are generated by the kernels of the stalk maps of the chart projections `W ×_X X_i → W`.
This file shows that they are one family: the ideal of the *first* is the ideal of the *second*.

This holds because the chart of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.ringEquiv_henselianLocalRing_quotient_ker_stalkMap_rep_snd` is the base
change `W ×_X X_i` and its chart morphism the projection to `W` — the very morphism
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.closedSubspaceBaseChangeChartProj` whose kernel the incidence statement
is about — so the two kernels are the kernel of one morphism.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_componentIdealFamily_ringEquiv_le_iff`: **the one family.**
  For closed subspaces `X_i ⊆ X` whose point sets are irreducible components of `|X|`, with
  points `ξ i` over `x`, a family of ideals `I i` of `A` with both `A ⧸ I i ≅ 𝒪^h_{X_i, ξ i}`
  and the incidence of the branches.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_componentIdealFamily_isReduced_ringKrullDim_eq_one_le_iff`:
  the same with the two ring-theoretic hypotheses of the additivity read off from the
  isomorphism, for components that are integral and locally Noetherian and carry a prime divisor
  through `x`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.exists_natCast_ord_sub_eq_finsum_components_mul`: **the additivity at
  `A = 𝒪^h_{Y, ξ}`** for `ξ` the generic point of a prime divisor of an algebraic space `Y`,
  with every hypothesis about the ring `A`, about the family of ideals and about the
  branch-to-component map discharged, the weights being the multiplicities of Stacks 0EE9 of the
  components, and the quotients `A ⧸ I i` presented as the henselian local rings
  `𝒪^h_{Y_i, ξ_i}` of the components.

## Implementation notes

The four instances making `A` a flat algebra over the local ring of the chart are restated here
at the `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.chartScheme` spelling: instance search does not pass between the
stalk of `V.scheme.left.1`, where `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.stalkAlgebra` puts it, and the stalk
of `chartScheme V.chart`, where the branch machinery of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Spaces.BranchesOverComponents` takes it, the intervening
definitions not being reducible.

